{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01AsaYRm41DNLRGxxh6JainU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q33 — Filter PII before data reaches LLM**:\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Concept:** Defense-in-depth pipeline using Microsoft Presidio at every data entry point (ingestion → vector index, query input, logs) — not just the final prompt\n- **Mechanism:** Two detection layers (rule-based regex/Luhn checksum + NER spaCy/BERT), four anonymization strategies compared (redaction / pseudonymization / masking / synthetic substitution / encryption) with when-to-use guidance\n- **Example:** Healthcare HIPAA triage agent — MedSpacy PHI recognizer, 18 entity types, session-scoped pseudonym lookup table, de-anonymize only in the on-prem display layer\n- **Scale angle:** Presidio as async sidecar microservice (10ms p95 SLO), SHA-256 content-hash cache to skip re-scanning identical chunks, domain BERT NER for false-negative mitigation\n- **Pitfalls:** (1) Only filtering at prompt time, missing ingestion + logs; (2) Recommending redaction-only without discussing coreference/coherence degradation; (3) Treating it as purely a prompt concern, ignoring the vector store surface"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":66101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12083560-950b-4ec5-b010-415837c6ee22","uuid":"32503d05-e531-4477-89b7-65d03a60e240"}
